# Shell Backgrounding

`block_until_ms` is a per-call tunable, not a fixed 30s. Pick a value based on
the command class. Default foreground; background is the exception.

## Policy by command class

| Command | `block_until_ms` | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `git status`, `git log`, `git diff`, `rg`, `sfa list --json` | default (30000) | finishes in seconds |
| `sfa backtest`, `sfa trials` | 120000 | usually 30–90s; wait for result |
| `sfa optimise --trials N` | `0` | minutes–hours; background immediately |
| `sfa walkforward` | `0` | long; background |
| `sfa sweep-single` | `0` | long; background |
| `sfa run --mode paper` | `0` | non-terminating; background |
| `python main.py` (Dash dev server) | `0` | non-terminating; background |
| `python -m pytest lib/tests/` (full) | `0` | noisy, long; background |
| `python -m pytest lib/tests/test_X.py` (single) | 120000 | usually <2min; wait |
| `uv sync`, `pip install` | 120000 | occasional slowness; wait |

## Rules

- **Never background commands <10s** — polling overhead exceeds the wall-clock
  benefit. Foreground is faster for `rg`, `git status`, `sfa list`.
- **Never use shell `&`** to background. Always set `block_until_ms: 0` so the
  harness tracks the process for cleanup and re-attach.
- **Never run `sleep` / `Start-Sleep` to "wait"** for a command. Either raise
  `block_until_ms` or poll the backgrounded shell with `AwaitShell`.
- **Background only self-contained work.** Backgrounded commands can't pause to
  ask clarifying questions. If a task needs interactive approval mid-run, keep
  it foreground.
- **Smoke-check after backgrounding.** When you spawn with `block_until_ms: 0`,
  do one status check by reading the output file to confirm it didn't fail to
  start. One check, not a poll loop.
- **Don't poll reflexively.** For fire-and-forget commands (tests, builds), let
  the completion notification fire. Only `AwaitShell` when the next step is
  blocked on the result.

## Anti-patterns

- Letting the 30s default expire on a known 10-minute `sfa optimise` — burns 30s
  for nothing. Set `block_until_ms: 0` up front.
- Backgrounding `rg foo` to "speed it up" — polling costs more than the command.
- `Start-Sleep 60` after kicking off a paper runner — use `AwaitShell` or just
  end the turn and rely on the completion notification.
